      "kicker": "Robotics Floor",
      "headline": "Robotics startups raised $27.6 billion in 2025, led by physical AI bets",
      "deck": "Funding doubled year over year across 1,009 deals, with robotics foundation models and general-purpose manipulation drawing the largest rounds.",
      "body": [
        "Robotics and physical AI startups raised a record $27.6 billion across 1,009 deals in 2025, more than double the prior year, according to PitchBook. The surge includes large early rounds for companies building robot foundation models and wheeled service robots for commercial environments.",
        "Dyna Robotics, which builds foundation models for service tasks in hotels, restaurants, and laundromats, raised a $120 million Series A within about a year of founding. Genesis AI emerged from stealth with a $105 million seed round for a wheeled robot that operates in commercial spaces without replicating the human body.",
        "Investor interest is concentrated in manufacturing, automotive, logistics, and healthcare, where firms are piloting robots to address labor costs and shortages. Figure AI reached a $39 billion valuation within three years by assembling auto parts in BMW factories, the fastest path to unicorn status in robotics history."
      ],
      "why": "The jump in deal volume and focus on robotics foundation models signals stronger near-term demand for manipulation and egocentric video datasets, especially from companies targeting service and light-industrial tasks rather than humanoid-only form factors.",
      "hard": "The report describes most physical AI companies as still in the founder-surge stage, meaning production deployments are limited and failure rates among startups remain high.",
